th1-surjection-curation-001+math1-bijection-curation-001+math1-union-curation-001+math1-proper-curation-001+math1-complement-curation-001+math1-complement-render-001+math1-division-curation-001+math1-reciprocal-curation-001+math1-inequality-curation-001+math1-inequality-feedback-001+math1-maximum-curation-001+math1-minimum-curation-001+math1-boundedset-curation-001+math1-endpoint-curation-001+audit-groups-20261027+topup-math-i-20261028+topup-math-ii-20261028+topup-pt-20261028+topup-math-iii-20261028","history_only":true,"curation_sha256":"402117cd2ecc28eaf6387aaefcadec5f0c0540f0912f8a96983845daf37ec8e2","concept_id":"Year-2/1a-Math-V-Advanced-Linear-Algebra/row-space.html","concept":{"concept_id":"Year-2/1a-Math-V-Advanced-Linear-Algebra/row-space.html","questions":[{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_row_space_b531716f_008","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"The row space $\\operatorname{Row}(A)$ of a real matrix $A$ is the span of its rows. A real $5\\times3$ matrix $A$ has three linearly independent columns. What is $\\dim \\operatorname{Row}(A)$?","options":["$5$","$2$","It cannot be found without the rows","$3$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"3a91e126dd7f03b6670f62a4","time_limit":30,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"replaced_after_academic_review"},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_row_space_b531716f_013","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $A$ be a real $m\\times n$ matrix. Which set equals its row space $\\operatorname{Row}(A)$, the span of the rows?","options":["$\\{A\\boldsymbol{y}\\colon\\boldsymbol{y}\\in\\mathbb{R}^n\\}$","$\\{A^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{y}\\colon\\boldsymbol{y}\\in\\mathbb{R}^m\\}$","$\\{\\boldsymbol{x}\\in\\mathbb{R}^n\\colon A\\boldsymbol{x}=\\boldsymbol{0}\\}$","$\\{\\boldsymbol{y}\\in\\mathbb{R}^m\\colon A^{\\top}\\boldsymbol{y}=\\boldsymbol{0}\\}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"16be382ed7630ebc4678480a","time_limit":30,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"replaced_after_academic_review"},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_row_space_b531716f_015","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"A real $4\\times4$ matrix has rows $\\boldsymbol{r}_1=(1,0,2,1)$, $\\boldsymbol{r}_2=(0,1,1,3)$, $\\boldsymbol{r}_3=\\boldsymbol{r}_1+\\boldsymbol{r}_2$ and $\\boldsymbol{r}_4=2\\boldsymbol{r}_1-\\boldsymbol{r}_2$. What is the dimension of its row space?","options":["$2$","$4$","$3$","$1$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"6f0963a672a3512392765165","time_limit":30,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"replaced_after_academic_review"},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_row_space_b531716f_016","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"For $A=\\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\\\0&0\\end{pmatrix}$, with row space $\\operatorname{span}\\{(1,0)\\}$, which operation on $A$ can change the row space?","options":["Swapping the two rows","Adding row $1$ to row $2$","Multiplying row $1$ by $5$","Swapping the two columns"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"14b4bfa1b943e9129d862b5d","time_limit":30,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"replaced_after_academic_review"},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_row_space_b531716f_017","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"For a real square matrix $A$, how is \\\"$A$ is symmetric\\\" related to \\\"the row space $\\operatorname{Row}(A)$ equals the column space $\\operatorname{Col}(A)$\\\"?","options":["Symmetric is sufficient but not necessary","Every matrix with equal row and column space is symmetric","The two conditions are equivalent","Symmetric is neither necessary nor sufficient"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"817938b4588d4dd22dbab0c9","time_limit":40,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"replaced_after_academic_review"},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_row_space_b531716f_018","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $B$ be $k\\times m$ and $A$ be $m\\times n$, both real. How is the row space of $BA$ related to the row space of $A$?","options":["It contains it, since $BA$ can have more rows than $A$","They are always equal, since $B$ only acts on the rows","It is contained in it, since each row of $BA$ combines rows of $A$","They are unrelated, since they lie in different spaces"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"fb544897e61091b3dfb9f442","time_limit":40,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"replaced_after_academic_review"},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_row_space_b531716f_019","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"For $A=\\begin{pmatrix}1&2&0&1\\\\2&4&1&3\\\\3&6&1&4\\end{pmatrix}$, whose reduced row echelon form has nonzero rows $(1,2,0,1)$ and $(0,0,1,1)$, row $3$ of $A$ equals row $1$ plus row $2$. For which right-hand sides $\\boldsymbol{b}=(b_1,b_2,b_3)^{\\top}$ is $A\\boldsymbol{x}=\\boldsymbol{b}$ consistent?","options":["Every $\\boldsymbol{b}\\in\\mathbb{R}^3$, since $\\operatorname{rank}A=2$","Exactly those with $b_3=b_1+b_2$","Exactly those with $b_3=0$","Exactly those with $b_1=b_2=b_3$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"45bbb5d750581d9ad62b650f","time_limit":40,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"replaced_after_academic_review"},{"id":"year_2_1a_math_v_advanced_linear_algebra_row_space_b531716f_020","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"For which real $k$ does $A=\\begin{pmatrix}1&2&1\\\\2&k&2\\\\1&2&1\\end{pmatrix}$ have a one-dimensional row space?","options":["$k=2$","$k=1$","No $k$: three nonzero rows span at least two dimensions","$k=4$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"76e504bd60ff16f73d1d0ad6","time_limit":40,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"replaced_after_academic_review"}]}}